{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And I will make your cities a ruin.</b> One might think — by the hand of man. But when He says, ״וַהֲשִׁמֹּתִי אֲנִי אֶת הָאָרֶץ״ — behold, man is stated. So how do I fulfill ״חָרְבָּה״? By passersby." "<b>And I will lay waste your sanctuaries.</b> One might think — from the offerings. But when He says, ״וְלֹא אָרִיחַ״, behold, offerings are stated. So how do I fulfill ״וַהֲשִׁמֹּתִי אֶת מִקְדְּשֵׁיכֶם״? From the גְּדוּדִיּוֹת — the companies of Israel that would consecrate themselves and assemble to come there. Behold, seven punishments: eating the flesh of sons and daughters, and destruction of the בָּמוֹת — behold two; cutting down of חַמָּנִים is no punishment in itself, but through the destruction of the roof-turrets the חַמָּנִים on the rooftops fall and are cut down — ״וְנָתַתִּי אֶת פִּגְרֵיכֶם״ וגוֹ׳, behold three; withdrawal of the Shechinah — four; destruction of cities; desolation of the Sanctuary from the גְּדוּדִיּוֹת; ״וְלֹא אָרִיחַ״ — offerings; behold seven."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "גְּדוּדִיּוֹת rendered 'companies' per Rashi's own gloss שַׁיָּרוֹת ('detachments/bands'). חַמָּנִים left untranslated as it is a technical term for cultic fixtures (possibly sun-pillars or incense altars); the precise identity is debated."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:51.200450928Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}